# Orbicrew workspace

Read `docs/development/AGENT_BOOTSTRAP.md` at session start for full onboarding.

## Layout

- `docs/leangine-office-docs/` — product & tech requirements (source of truth for *what*)
- `docs/development/` — phase plan, manual tests, tracker (source of truth for *process*)
- `repos/` — nested org git repos where product code lives
- `resources/` — master-only assets (`logos/`, `stitch_orbicrew_ui_ux_guide/`, `orbicrew_dev_infra/`)
- `local/` — private scratch — **never read unless the user explicitly asks**

## Ownership

- Master workspace git = personal GitHub `https://github.com/meetrakib/orbicrew_master` (docs + agent config + `resources/`)
- `repos/*` = Leangine org GitHub — commit code inside the nested repo, not into master
  - web: `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-web` (tenant UI + Orbit View)
  - admin: `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-admin` (platform operator console)
  - api: `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-api`
  - channels: `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-channels`
  - infra: `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-infra`

## Local infra

- Shared deps (Postgres+pgvector, Redis): `resources/orbicrew_dev_infra/` via `docker compose up -d`
- Develop api / web / admin / channels **natively** — do not run app services in Docker during development

## Nested repo isolation

When editing under `repos/<name>/`, never reference master-only paths (`docs/`, `resources/`, `local/`, workspace layout). Nested repos must stay standalone. See `nested-repos.mdc`.

## Coding principles

- Follow language/framework best practices for the stack in use.
- Prefer reusable shared abstractions (DRY, shared packages/patterns) over copy-paste across services — extract when duplication is real, not speculative.

## Workflow

1. Before feature work → follow `docs/development/phase_by_phase_development_plan.md`
2. After a development slice → update `docs/development/manual-test-guide.md` if needed
3. After completing work → append to `docs/development/development-tracker.md`

Do not implement product features at the workspace root.

## Branches (nested repos)

`main` (prod) · `stage` · `dev` (default active work)
